    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Henry Kee & Son are thrilled to present for sale this superb five bedroom detached home offering an impressive 3050 sq. ft. approx. of luxury accommodation. Nestled in a substantial site in excess of one acre, the property enjoys views of Lough Alaan and over Ballybofey & Stranorlar Golf Course. Set in an excellent location on the N13 National Primary Route connecting Stranorlar to Derry, and within a few minutes of Stranorlar Main Street, this residence places an array of amenities at your doorstep, from shops, schools, churches, cafes and bars to the numerous sports clubs including, GAA and soccer clubs, Athletic and tennis clubs and cycling and golf club. Decorated in a heritage style, internal accommodation includes Reception Hall, Sitting Room, Living Room, Conservatory, Kitchen, Dining Room, Utility, Ground floor Bedroom and WC, whilst the first floor offers a spacious landing and four spacious double bedrooms and bathroom. The main bedroom features an en-suite shower room, and all bedrooms contain either walk-in wardrobes or a suite of fitted robes. The property includes an integral garage, a gated entrance with tarmac drive up to the house and paved parking area to the front and rear. The property has been MICA tested and received a very good result. Viewing of the stunning home is highly recommended, strictly by prior appointment only. Don't miss the opportunity to make this exquisite property your own."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "<br><br>\nReception Hall - 4.9m x 3.8m <br>Mahogany return staircase. \nStained glass picture windows either side of the front door. \nDouble doors with stained glass top panels leading to sitting room. \nDado rail.\nTiffany style ceiling light. \nTwo wall lights.\nCeiling rose and cornicing. \nFloor carpeted. <br><br><br>\nSitting Room - 5.3m x 4.8m* <br>Installed gas fire with mahogany surround and matching over-mantle. \nTwo windows to front with views over Lough Alaan.\nCustom-made luxury curtains with swag valance. \nCeiling rose and cornicing. \nPolished brass and clear crystal chandelier. \nCarpeted to match reception hall.\n*maximum measurement. <br><br><br>\nLiving Room - 4.8m x 3.5m <br>Open fire with mahogany surround and matching over-mantle. \nTwo windows to front with views over Lough Alaan.\nCeiling rose and cornicing. \nPolished brass and clear crystal chandelier. \nDouble doors with stained glass top panels leading to conservatory. \nFloor carpeted. <br><br><br>\nConservatory - 5.4m x 4.3m <br>Edwardian style. \nPatio doors leading to garden. \nCeiling fan light fitting. \nSolid timber floor. <br><br><br>\nKitchen - 4.8m x 4.7m <br>Solid timber high and low level kitchen units with tiles between. \nIntegrated fridge/freezer. \nIntegrated electric double oven and electric hob. \nGable window over sink.\nDouble doors leading to dining room.\nDoor to rear hall and door to reception hall. \nSix down-lighters. \nCeiling coving. \nFloor tiled. <br><br><br>\nDining Room - 3.7m x 3.4m <br>Window to rear. \nCeiling rose and cornicing.\nPolished brass and clear crystal chandelier. \nCarpeted to match reception hall. <br><br><br>\nRear Hall / Utility - 3.3m x 1.7m* <br>High and low level kitchen units, tiled between.\nPlumbed for washing machine and tumbledryer. \nWalk-in hotpress. \nCloak room / broom cupboard. \nDoor to integrated garage. \nBack door. \nFloor tiled to match kitchen. \n* maximum measurement. <br><br><br>\nGround Floor Bedroom - 3.4m x 3m <br>Window to rear. \nCeiling rose and coving. \nFloor carpeted. <br><br><br>\nWC - 1.6m x 1.3m <br>WHB and WC.\nWalls tiled to 3/4 height. \nWindow. \nFloor tiled. <br><br><br>\nLanding - 5.7m x 3.8m <br>Bay window to front with views of Lough Alaan and local golf course. \nDado rail. \nCeiling rose and cornicing.\nPolished brass and clear crystal chandelier. \nWooden floor. <br><br><br>\nMain Bedroom - 4.8m x 4.3m <br>Gable window.\nFitted wardrobes and drawers.\nSolid timber floor. \n\nEn-Suite:\n2.6m x 1.3m\nWC, WHB and spacious shower with electric shower unit. \nWindow to rear. \nWalls tiled to 3/4 height. \nFloor tiled. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Three - 4.8m x 3.3m <br>Wall-to-wall fitted wardrobes. \nTwo windows to front with views over Lough Alaan.\nSolid timber floor. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Four - 4.8m x 3.1m <br>Walk-in wardrobe measuring 2.2m x 1.1m with window and radiator. \nTwo windows to front with views over Lough Alaan.\nSolid timber floor. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Five - 4.4m x 3.6m <br>Walk-in wardrobe measuring 2.6m x 1.4m with radiator. \nRear window. \nFloor carpeted. <br><br><br>\nBathroom - 2.6m x 2.5m <br>WC, WHB and bath.\nSeparate shower with electric shower unit. \nWalls tiled to 3/4 height. \nFloor tiled. <br><br><br>\nIntegral Garage - 5.3m x 4.5m <br>Up and over vehicular door. <br><br>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Stunning detached home in superb location.\nGenerous site measuring 0.47 hec/1.16 acres approx.\nArray of amenities on your doorstep.\nImpressive reception hall with mahogany return staircase.\nSpacious Sitting room with installed gas fire and splendid views of Lough Alaan.\nSeparate family room also with open fire in a feature mahogany fireplace and views over Lough Alaan.\nFive large double bedrooms, Principal bedroom with ensuite shower room.\nMany luxury, custom made, window dressings.\nOil fired central heating.\nIntegral garage.\nMica tested with very good result.\nPrivate landscaped gardens with surrounding lawns, bushes and trees with excellent degree of privacy, tarmac drive from gated entrance leads to paved area around house.\nConvenient commuting distance to many parts of the province and onto the main arterial route to Dublin."
      },
